{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_002, 0.6352 acc) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted + multiprofile. Across experiments, multiprofile > singleprofile, vit_l > resnet50, avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat, and pca_n2000 >> scgpt (0.635 vs 0.518). The only untested dimension at the known-best settings is the RNA encoder: scvi_n200. This experiment tests whether a learned VAE-based 200-dim RNA representation can match or exceed PCA-2000 while retaining the strong image and fusion pipeline. It is the highest-value exploration because it is the sole remaining untested axis with all other hyperparameters fixed at their empirically best values; a positive result would yield a new best configuration, while a negative result definitively confirms pca_n2000 as optimal and lets the remaining 2 experiments focus on fine-tuning other aspects. Expected cost is moderate (~7–10 GPU hours), comparable to config_002, since the architecture is identical apart from the RNA encoder (a small 200-dim VAE), keeping total budget well within limits."
}

